++/// The size of a pooled block, at most the device's `maxMemoryAllocationSize`. Each pool keeps
++/// half a block free ([`keep_room`]), so the blocks a process holds before it places anything
++/// grow with this size times its pools. With 64 MiB blocks an iOS client's empty room alone
++/// nearly filled its 256 MiB GPU window; a request past half a block is still dedicated.
++pub(super) const BLOCK_BYTES: u64 = 16 << 20;
